  "title": "Account, routes & story ownership",
  "md": "# Account, routes & story ownership\n\n## Routes (`lib/routes.ts` is the single source of truth)\n| URL | Page |\n|---|---|\n| `/` | Search landing (or the story page if a story is loaded) |\n| `/story/[id]` | A story's own page — refresh-safe and shareable; story cards link here |\n| `/dashboard`, `/profile/[userId]` | Home dashboard, public profile |\n| `/reading-history` | Every story read, grouped by date, paginated |\n| `/analytics` | Speed / comprehension charts |\n| `/history` | Past test attempts (also in the hamburger menu) |\n| `/settings` | Theme, reading font, reading speed |\n\nNavbar: the reading-mode toggle and the story-title link were removed; the profile menu rows are real routes.\n\n## Story ownership\nAn uploaded story belongs to the user whose personal library holds it.\n`SessionManager.findCustomStoryOwner(id)` finds that user; `getContentAuthorId` asks it first (via\n`registerCustomStoryOwnerResolver`, wired in `lib/session/composition.ts`) and only falls back to the\ndemo mapping for built-in stories. The resolver is injected so `contentMeta` never imports the session\nlayer (which depends on the store that imports `contentMeta` — a cycle otherwise). Test: `npm test`.\n\n## Profile photo\n`lib/avatar.ts` centre-crops to 256px JPEG; `devDataStore.setAvatar/getAvatar` persist it (own photo only).\n`components/ui/Avatar.tsx` shows photo → initial → icon; used in the navbar, profile menu and profile page.\nUpload/remove: profile menu or profile page (`useAvatarUpload`).\n\n## Edit story\n`EditStoryModal` reuses the Add-story modal parts (`StoryFormParts`, `StoryCoverPicker`, `QuestionsInput`,\nrich editor) so both look identical. Replaced/removed cover videos are deleted only when the edit is saved.\n\n## Navbar layout & audience section\n- Navbar: left = hamburger menu + company name; right = notifications, dark-mode switch (`ThemeSwitch`), profile. The centre slot still hosts the search box / reading timer.\n- Landing \"For every ambitious mind.\" is an Apple-style carousel (`components/Landing/AudienceMarquee.tsx`): tall dark cards, caption below with a bold lead, previous/next buttons bottom-right, scroll-snap and touch swipe.\n\n## Profile button, logout, carousel\n- The navbar profile button opens your profile page directly (no dropdown). Dashboard / Reading history / Analytics / Past test attempts / Settings are quick links on your own profile page; **Log out** is at the bottom of the hamburger menu.\n- Landing story carousel: translucent glass covers sit outside the two vertical guide lines (under the arrows); each card's arrow button starts auto-scroll reading at `/reader` (`StoryCard arrowStartsReader`), everything else on the card is unchanged.\n",
  "titleHi": "Account, routes और story ownership",
  "hi": {
   "title": "Account, routes और story ownership",
   "md": "# Account, routes और story ownership\n\n## Routes (`lib/routes.ts` ही single source of truth है)\n| URL | Page |\n|---|---|\n| `/` | Search landing (या story page अगर कोई story loaded है) |\n| `/story/[id]` | किसी story का अपना page — refresh-safe और shareable; story cards यहीं link करते हैं |\n| `/dashboard`, `/profile/[userId]` | Home dashboard, public profile |\n| `/reading-history` | पढ़ी गई हर story, तारीख के अनुसार grouped, paginated |\n| `/analytics` | Speed / comprehension charts |\n| `/history` | पिछले test attempts (hamburger menu में भी) |\n| `/settings` | Theme, reading font, reading speed |\n\nNavbar: reading-mode toggle और story-title link हटा दिए गए; profile menu की rows असली routes हैं।\n\n## Story ownership\nUpload की गई story उस user की होती है जिसकी personal library में वह है।\n`SessionManager.findCustomStoryOwner(id)` उस user को ढूँढता है; `getContentAuthorId` पहले इसी से पूछता है\n(`registerCustomStoryOwnerResolver` के ज़रिए, जो `lib/session/composition.ts` में जुड़ा है) और सिर्फ़ built-in stories के लिए\ndemo mapping पर वापस जाता है। Resolver inject किया जाता है ताकि `contentMeta` कभी session\nlayer को import न करे (जो उस store पर निर्भर है जो `contentMeta` को import करता है — वरना cycle बन जाएगा)। Test: `npm test`।\n\n## Profile photo\n`lib/avatar.ts` 256px JPEG में centre-crop करता है; `devDataStore.setAvatar/getAvatar` इसे persist करते हैं (सिर्फ़ अपनी photo)।\n`components/ui/Avatar.tsx` photo → initial → icon दिखाता है; navbar, profile menu और profile page में इस्तेमाल होता है।\nUpload/remove: profile menu या profile page (`useAvatarUpload`)।\n\n## Edit story\n`EditStoryModal` Add-story modal के हिस्सों (`StoryFormParts`, `StoryCoverPicker`, `QuestionsInput`,\nrich editor) को दोबारा इस्तेमाल करता है ताकि दोनों बिल्कुल एक जैसे दिखें। बदले/हटाए गए cover videos सिर्फ़ तब delete होते हैं जब edit save किया जाए।\n\n## Navbar layout और audience section\n- Navbar: बायाँ = hamburger menu + company name; दायाँ = notifications, dark-mode switch (`ThemeSwitch`), profile। बीच का slot अब भी search box / reading timer रखता है।\n- Landing का \"For every ambitious mind.\" एक Apple-style carousel है (`components/Landing/AudienceMarquee.tsx`): लंबे dark cards, नीचे bold शुरुआत वाला caption, नीचे दाईं ओर previous/next buttons, scroll-snap और touch swipe।\n\n## Profile button, logout, carousel\n- Navbar का profile button सीधे आपका profile page खोलता है (कोई dropdown नहीं)। Dashboard / Reading history / Analytics / Past test attempts / Settings आपके अपने profile page पर quick links हैं; **Log out** hamburger menu के सबसे नीचे है।\n- Landing story carousel: पारदर्शी glass covers दो खड़ी guide lines के बाहर (arrows के नीचे) हैं; हर card का arrow button `/reader` पर auto-scroll reading शुरू करता है (`StoryCard arrowStartsReader`), card पर बाकी सब कुछ वैसा ही है।\n"
  }
